---
import '../styles/tokens.css';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import AppCta from '../components/AppCta.astro';
import WeekDiary from '../components/WeekDiary.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';

// Why Streaq exists: a short, public reflection of the product principles in
// proj2/product/principles.md. Every promise here must be true of the shipped
// app: this page is a commitment, not a roadmap.
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Why we’re building Streaq"
      description="We are what we repeatedly do. Streaq is an honest diary of your week, kept with a few close friends who’ll notice."
      previewDescription="Don’t tell me about your priorities. Show me your last week’s diary."
      path="/manifesto"
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <SiteHeader />

    <div class="col">
      <main>
        <h1>
          <span>We are what we repeatedly do.</span>
          <span>Excellence, then, is not an act,</span> <span>but a habit.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="attr">Will Durant</p>

        <p>
          Not what we say we are, or what we plan to become. Not the priorities we’d list
          if someone asked. We are what we make time for, day after day.
        </p>

        <div class="diary"><WeekDiary /></div>

        <blockquote>
          <span>Don’t tell me about your priorities.</span>
          <span>Show me your last week’s diary.</span>
        </blockquote>

        <p>
          Streaq is that diary. One tap a day, done or not. No scores, no spin, just an
          honest week, clear enough to change.
        </p>
        <p>
          And because a promise is easier to keep when someone’s watching, you keep it with
          a few close friends. Not followers, not strangers. The people who’d notice, there
          to back you up rather than judge.
        </p>
        <p>
          No ads, no tracking, no games. Just the habits that matter, kept with the people
          who matter.
        </p>

        <p class="last">What gets measured, gets improved.</p>
        <div class="cta"><AppCta /></div>
      </main>
    </div>

    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* One column, one left edge, one spacing scale (16 / 32 / 64). */
  .col {
    --s1: 16px;
    --s2: 32px;
    --s3: 64px;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 60px var(--s3);
  }

  main {
    padding-top: var(--s2);
  }

  /* Three sizes only: headline quote, quote, body. All one family (the body
     face); the display face is reserved for the brand and the home hero. */
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 600;
    /* Three fixed lines, one per clause, on every screen. The longest is
       13.4em, so the size is capped to always fit the column (with ~4%
       headroom): 40px on desktop, smaller on phones, never a stray wrap. */
    font-size: min(40px, calc((100vw - 56px) / 13.9));
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1 span,
  blockquote span {
    display: block;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .attr {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--mute);
    margin: var(--s1) 0 40px;
  }
  blockquote {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 500;
    /* Two fixed lines; the longest is 14.6em. Same capping as the h1. */
    font-size: min(28px, calc((100vw - 56px) / 15.2));
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s2);
  }
  p {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--sub);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s1);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .last {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }

  .diary {
    margin: var(--s3) 0;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: var(--s2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .col {
      padding: 0 28px var(--s3);
    }
    p {
      font-size: 17px;
    }
  }
</style>
